			"date": "2024-02-14T16:58:55.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Interestingly, having just heard from <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@castastrophe\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>castastrophe</span></a></span> about Adobe's focus on web components and design systems, it seems like we need high profile companies like Adobe to lead the way demonstrating that the native web is the future.</p><p>I don't know if it'll take a Responsive Web Design &gt; Boston Globe moment for developers and companies to take a 2nd look, but the market needs to be shook up and presented practical examples of a better way!</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
