			"date": "2024-02-14T17:32:44.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Not every conversation about front-end development has to be about industrial grade tooling, of course, but:</p><p>- Who’s building things At Scale™ with Eleventy (et al)?<br>- How did they successfully pitch that tool chain?<br>- What benefits are clients seeing on the other side?</p><p>would all be lovely things for standards-friendly advocates to reference or point to when having their own internal discussions ☺️</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "111931063111248825",
			"parentId": "111931008518873813",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@aaadaaam/111931062868676811",
			"author": {
				"name": "Adam Stoddard",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@aaadaaam",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/303/181/435/692/045/original/3fd463116c0fb80b.png"
			},
			"date": "2024-02-14T17:41:17.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://front-end.social/@sarajw\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>sarajw</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> these are all better answers than what I've had!</p><p>I think the thing I'm getting at is that React has super polished, outcome focused (here's what you need to know to get a job / build things people will pay for) courseware like <a href=\"https://react.gg\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" translate=\"no\" target=\"_blank\"><span class=\"invisible\">https://</span><span class=\"\">react.gg</span><span class=\"invisible\"></span></a> and the platform-centric approach doesn't. If employers want React *and* React has an easier on-ramp then new folks are going to pick it.</p><p>(I feel like I'm convincing myself to make courseware oh no)</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
